# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker build context control.
#
# Both Dockerfiles build from the PROJECT ROOT (so shared/ is in context), and
# the root is ~3.8 GB: local/slm/models/*.gguf is 2.3 GB, .git is 1.6 GB, and
# cloud/backend/base_documents/ holds 17 MB of source PDFs. The cloud image
# needs none of it. Without this file every build — including every CI build —
# uploads all 3.8 GB to the builder before the first instruction runs.
#
# Strategy: deny everything, then allow back only what the Dockerfiles COPY.
# Intermediate directories are re-included explicitly because an excluded
# directory is pruned before its children are ever considered.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

*

# shared/ — imported by the cloud app (env, logging, masking, chunking, hybrid)
!shared

# cloud/backend/{app,requirements*.txt} — the service itself.
# Deliberately NOT included: base_documents/ and chunks_staging.json (ingestion
# inputs, run once from the analyst machine) and the 1_/2_ ingestion scripts.
!cloud
cloud/*
!cloud/backend
cloud/backend/*
!cloud/backend/app
!cloud/backend/requirements.txt
!cloud/backend/requirements-lambda.txt

# Belt and braces: never ship secrets or caches, even from inside the
# allow-listed trees above.
**/.env
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
